    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`cmd_on_key()` tests the key it was handed against the literal string `'<MouseMove>'`, but at that point `typed` still holds raw key bytes. Thus the comparison never holds and the branch its own comment describes is dead. Moving the mouse over an expanded cmdline collapses it.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nTranslate the key once, up front, so every comparison in the function sees the same form.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-06T16:37:29Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
                "html": {
                    "href": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41732#discussion_r3944483016"
                },
                "pull_request": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/41732"
                },
                "self": {
                    "href": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/pulls/comments/3944483016"
                }
            },
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "this will probably yield a \"immediately succeeded\" warning in the test logs (i didn't check).\n\nbut anyway, can we just add a `api.nvim_input_mouse('move', '', '', 0, 0, 3)` in the existing test(s) ? presumably here https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/eb1a6d30c3ba535f917ad969b9d9228db9f73219/test/functional/ui/messages2_spec.lua#L583-L584",
            "commit_id": "eb1a6d30c3ba535f917ad969b9d9228db9f73219",
            "created_at": "2026-09-06T15:55:29Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -301,6 +301,30 @@ describe('messages2', function()\n     ]])\n   end)\n \n+  it('mouse movement does not dismiss expanded messages', function()\n+    command('set mousemoveevent | echo \"foo\\nbar\"')\n+    local expanded = [[\n+      ^                                                     |\n+      {1:~                                                    }|*10\n+      {3:                                                     }|\n+      foo                                                  |\n+      bar                                                  |\n+    ]]\n+    screen:expect(expanded)\n+\n+    -- Moving the mouse is not a key press that dismisses messages.\n+    api.nvim_input_mouse('move', '', '', 0, 0, 3)\n+    screen:expect(expanded)",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41732#discussion_r3944483016",
